---
title: "FilePizza share, status, and stop"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  s0: Checking the local file
  s1: Waiting for a link
  s2: Share failed
  s3: Stopping the share
  s4: Share command timed out
  s5: Share stopped
  s6: Link available
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: the file is accepted
  s0 --> s2: the file is rejected
  s1 --> s3: the sender interrupts the command or the sender requests a stop
  s1 --> s4: the share deadline passes
  s1 --> s2: the background worker exits or the share fails
  s3 --> s2: the background worker exits or the share fails
  s4 --> s2: the background worker exits or the share fails
  s1 --> s5: the background worker exits
  s1 --> s6: the command prints the link or the share deadline passes [status can show the link]
  s3 --> s5: the background worker exits or the background worker stops
  s4 --> s5: the background worker exits
  s4 --> s6: the link becomes available
  s6 --> s5: the background worker exits
  s6 --> s2: the share fails
  s4 --> s3: the sender requests a stop
  s6 --> s3: the sender requests a stop
